1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,200
Supplier payments get stolen by fake
bank-detail emails or paid too early.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,100
Dockside: a NEAR escrow that pays only
the signed account, after inspection.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:10,900
Web app on the local stack, simulated
chain: the buyer drafts one agreement.

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:15,300
It binds the payout account, inspector,
risk resolver and evidence policy.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:21,244
The supplier checks the buyer's signature,
countersigns, and the escrow registers it.

6
00:00:21,344 --> 00:00:25,844
Both parties signed one terms digest;
the payout is bound to one account.

7
00:00:25,944 --> 00:00:30,844
Inspector uploads the report and photos;
the isolated attestor signs the manifest.

8
00:00:30,844 --> 00:00:35,527
The named inspector signs PASS;
the simulated escrow records it.

9
00:00:35,627 --> 00:00:41,027
The buyer locks the value and approves;
the review names the bound recipient.

10
00:00:41,027 --> 00:00:46,177
Release can go only to the bound
supplier account (10 NEAR, simulated).

11
00:00:46,277 --> 00:00:50,277
PAID only after the reconciler reads
the chain receipt (simulated chain).

12
00:00:50,477 --> 00:00:55,277
Real run on NEAR testnet, in USDC:
escrow3 paid the supplier exactly 5 USDC.

13
00:00:55,277 --> 00:00:59,877
Paid, hold, refusal and refund: all four
journeys ran on NEAR testnet in USDC.

14
00:01:00,077 --> 00:01:04,877
Six attacks, six on-chain refusals,
each a real NEAR testnet transaction.

15
00:01:04,877 --> 00:01:09,477
Then the same trade completed:
exactly 5 USDC to the bound supplier.

16
00:01:09,677 --> 00:01:14,877
Live attack console: a real trade holds
2 test USDC in escrow3 on NEAR testnet.

17
00:01:14,877 --> 00:01:20,277
Five recorded attacks from an account with
no authority, read back from NEAR.

18
00:01:20,277 --> 00:01:25,421
Every attempt refused by the contract;
funds unchanged: still 2.00 USDC held.

19
00:01:25,621 --> 00:01:29,921
Proof page: your browser reads the escrow
contract live from NEAR testnet.

20
00:01:29,921 --> 00:01:34,054
Pass: all 63 checks, read live
at a final NEAR testnet block.

21
00:01:34,254 --> 00:01:38,754
Receipt page: a paid trade, re-verified
against NEAR testnet on every visit.

22
00:01:38,754 --> 00:01:42,808
All 9 checks pass: audited build, ledger,
inspection and the release transaction.

23
00:01:43,008 --> 00:01:49,308
pnpm judge: one command runs the tests and
re-reads both escrows on NEAR testnet.

24
00:01:49,308 --> 00:01:55,877
Real run on a fresh clone: 90 passed,
0 failed, 1 skipped (mainnet).

25
00:01:56,177 --> 00:02:02,677
NEAR testnet only; mainnet not deployed.
github.com/gnanam1990/dockside-near
